DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssuuppeerriioo set of functions are used for managing Super I/O devices.
     The functions provide support for raw configuration access, locating de‐
     vices, device information, and device configuration.

   TThhee ccoonnttrroolllleerr iinntteerrffaaccee
     The ssuuppeerriioo__vveennddoorr() function is used to get a vendor of the Super I/O
     controller _d_e_v.  Possible return values are SUPERIO_VENDOR_ITE and
     SUPERIO_VENDOR_NUVOTON.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__ddeevviidd() function is used to get a device ID of the Super I/O
     controller _d_e_v.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__rreevviidd() function is used to get a revision ID of the Super
     I/O controller _d_e_v.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__ffiinndd__ddeevv() function is used to find a device on the
     superio(4) bus, specified by _d_e_v, that has the requested type and logical
     device number.  Either of those, but not both, can be a wildcard.  Sup‐
     ported types are SUPERIO_DEV_GPIO, SUPERIO_DEV_HWM, and SUPERIO_DEV_WDT.
     The wildcard value for _t_y_p_e is SUPERIO_DEV_NONE.  The wildcard value for
     _l_d_n is -1.

   TThhee ddeevviiccee iinntteerrffaaccee
     The ssuuppeerriioo__rreeaadd() function is used to read data from the Super I/O con‐
     figuration register of the device _d_e_v.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__wwrriittee() function is used to write data to the Super I/O con‐
     figuration register of the device _d_e_v.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__ddeevv__eennaabbllee(), ssuuppeerriioo__ddeevv__ddiissaabbllee(), and
     ssuuppeerriioo__ddeevv__eennaabblleedd() functions are used to enable, disable, or check
     status of the device _d_e_v.  The _m_a_s_k parameter selects sub-functions of a
     device that supports them.  For devices that do not have sub-functions,
     _m_a_s_k should be set to 1.

   TThhee aacccceessssoorr iinntteerrffaaccee
     The ssuuppeerriioo__ggeett__ddmmaa() is used to get a DMA channel number configured for
     the device _d_e_v.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__ggeett__iioobbaassee() is used to get a base I/O port configured for
     the device _d_e_v.  The device may expose additional or alternative configu‐
     ration access via the I/O ports.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__ggeett__iirrqq() is used to get an interrupt number configured for
     the device _d_e_v.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__ggeett__llddnn() is used to get a Logical Device Number of the de‐
     vice _d_e_v.

     The ssuuppeerriioo__ggeett__ttyyppee() is used to get a type of the device _d_e_v.

